# SPPLPF Trivy Vulnerability Exception Configuration
# Reference: docs/security/vulnerability-triage-register.md
# Policy: Blanket ignore rules are strictly forbidden. Every entry must declare
# CVE ID, affected component, applicability rationale, owner, and review expiry date.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-56857
# Component: Go standard library os/internal/syscall/windows in /usr/local/bin/gosu (postgres:17.11-alpine)
# Severity: CRITICAL
# Finding Type: Non-applicable OS component
# Applicability Evidence: Windows directory junction flaw; internal/syscall/windows is not compiled into or reachable in Linux ELF binary.
# Owner: security-team@spplpf
# Expiry: 2026-12-31
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-56857

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-39821
# Component: golang.org/x/net/idna flagged against /usr/local/bin/gosu (postgres:17.11-alpine)
# Severity: CRITICAL
# Finding Type: Unimported sub-repository package
# Applicability Evidence: Punycode normalization flaw in x/net/idna. gosu source code only invokes syscall setuid/setgid/execvp and does not import x/net/idna.
# Owner: security-team@spplpf
# Expiry: 2026-12-31
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-39821

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2025-68121
# Component: Go crypto/tls in /usr/local/bin/gosu (postgres:17.11-alpine)
# Severity: CRITICAL
# Finding Type: Dead code path
# Applicability Evidence: TLS certificate authority session resumption flaw. gosu does not establish network connections or perform TLS handshakes.
# Owner: security-team@spplpf
# Expiry: 2026-12-31
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2025-68121

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
